--TEST--
A `foreach` with a key over a subject that has only `Iterable` or `Iterator`, such as a `Core\ObjectSet` or a user `Iterable<int>`, does not compile — `rule:iteration/keyed-interfaces`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:iteration/keys-and-values-from-a-map
final class Tag {
    public string $name;

    public function constructor(string $name) {
        $this->name = $name;
    }
}

final class Countdown implements Iterable<int> {
    public function iterate(): Iterator<int> {
        yield 2;
        yield 1;
    }
}

// A set has values but no keys, so `$k =>` does not compile.
Core\ObjectSet<Tag> $tags = new Core\ObjectSet<Tag>();
foreach ($tags as var $k => Tag $tag) {
}

// This class implements only `Iterable<int>`, so it has no keys either.
foreach (new Countdown() as var $i => int $n) {
}
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0444]: an `Iterable`/`Iterator` subject has no key to bind
   --> case.nvs:20:19
%A
error[E0444]: an `Iterable`/`Iterator` subject has no key to bind
   --> case.nvs:24:29
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
